# wakir-persona-engine REAL — Sprint-Pengine-14 / Tag-52
# Pre-KW-24-Final-Consolidation, image tag
# ``0.5.2-final-pre-cutover``.
#
# Tag-52 final consolidation (Sprint-Pengine-14, 2026-05-19)
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Tag-52 is the Pre-KW-24-Final consolidation marker. The image
# bump from ``0.5.1-pre-cutover`` to ``0.5.2-final-pre-cutover`` is
# a **manifest-and-metadata-only** marker — no new BackendDecision
# record, no flag rename, no flag-default flip, no crate-version
# bump. The 10-component inventory, the consistent
# ``WAKIR_*_BACKEND`` ENV-flag schema, and the 15-crate pin pack
# are all byte-stable vs. 0.5.1-pre-cutover (Tag-48 PR #313). The
# 0.5.2-final marker absorbs four Tag-48..51 sources:
#
#   * Tag-48 PR #313 — bridge-audit-writer wire-in (record #10).
#   * Tag-50 PR #320 — v0.4.2 DRIFT-S4 reconciliation patch
#     (Pin-Pack as SoT for spec §4.1 ENV-flag schema).
#   * Tag-51 PR #327 — 10-Decision-Engine-Resilience suite
#     (36 hermetic tests pinned-by-reference as the cutover-
#     window resilience-substrate-pin).
#   * Tag-51 PR #329 — legacy ``WAKIR_PE_*_BACKEND`` migration-
#     detector (Reza substrate; warn-no-fallback posture).
#
# 0.5.2-final-pre-cutover is the last pre-cutover image before the
# Phase-3c cutover window opens in KW 24. Operators rotate via
# Quadlet image-tag bump (Operator-Hand). The Tag-48 0.5.1-pre-cutover
# manifest + pin-pack + Tag-45 0.5.0-pre-cutover artefacts stay on
# disk as historical anchors for the Doppelbetrieb regression-
# comparison baseline.
#
# Tag-48 wire-in (Sprint-Pengine-14, 2026-05-19, absorbed)
# --------------------------------------------------------
# Tag-48 promotes the previously-held-back 10th BackendDecision
# (bridge-audit-writer; manifest 0.5.0-pre-cutover §5) into the
# Stage-1 boot fan-out. The 10-component inventory, the consistent
# ``WAKIR_*_BACKEND`` ENV-flag schema, and the 15-crate cross-
# language pin pack are now anchored in
# ``wirelang/persona_engine/MANIFEST-0.5.1-pre-cutover.md`` (joined
# with its YAML counterpart at
# ``infra/persona-engine/pin-pack-0.5.1-pre-cutover.yaml``).
#
# 0.5.1-pre-cutover is a **strict superset** of 0.5.0-pre-cutover:
# no BackendDecision rename, no flag-default flip, the boot order
# for records #1–9 is preserved byte-for-byte. The only observable
# change is one additional ``backend-decision`` JSON line at the
# tail of every cold-start audit log (record #10 with default-
# python posture). The Phase-3a 0.5.0-pre-cutover artefacts (the
# Tag-45 manifest + pin pack) stay on disk as historical anchors
# for the Doppelbetrieb gate's regression-comparison baseline.
# Operators rotate via Quadlet image-tag bump (Operator-Hand).
#
# Tag-45 pre-cutover consolidation (Sprint-Pengine-14, 2026-05-18)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Tag-45 closed the engine side of the Phase-3a/3b Doppelbetrieb
# cutover preparation at nine components. See the Tag-45 manifest
# at ``wirelang/persona_engine/MANIFEST-0.5.0-pre-cutover.md`` for
# the historical anchor; Tag-48 supersedes it but the file remains
# in-tree as the regression-comparison baseline.
#
# Bug-42 fix (Sprint-Pengine-13)
# ------------------------------
# 0.4.2-pilot (Sprint-Pengine-12) wired the CLI-async-dispatch path but
# the live-pilot engine still did not receive published Auftrags-
# messages on the canonical subject. Root cause: the
# ``NatsSubscribeLoop.run_with_iterator`` polled
# ``msg_iter.__anext__()`` via ``asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout=0.5)``;
# every 500ms timeout cancelled the inner nats-py ``get_task`` mid-
# flight, silently dropping any message that had just landed in the
# pending-queue. 0.5.0-pilot fixes this by:
#
#   1. Replacing the wait_for-poll with an ``asyncio.wait`` race
#      between a persistent next-msg-task and the stop-event.
#   2. Adding a ``subscribe-mode-selector`` env-var
#      (``WAKIR_NATS_SUBSCRIBE_MODE``) with three modes:
#        * ``core-callback`` (default) — nats-py callback subscribe;
#          avoids the iterator-cancellation surface entirely.
#        * ``core-iterator`` — backward-compat path; safe with the fix.
#        * ``jetstream-pull`` — Phase-2 durable-consumer substrate
#          (opt-in; replay-capable, ack-required).
#
# The CLI-async-dispatch log now emits ``subscribe_mode`` so the
# live-smoke operator can verify which path the container took.

# wakir-persona-engine REAL — Sprint-Pengine-10, image tag ``0.4.0-pilot``.
#
# Substrate scope (0.4.0-pilot)
# -----------------------------
# Sprint-Pengine-10 closes the input-side gap discovered during the
# 0.3.0-pilot Live-Engine-Swap (only heartbeat + spawn-init audit, no
# task-input plumbing). 0.4.0-pilot wires:
#
#   - OI-PEFR-6: real NATS-subscribe-loop on
#     ``wakir.<env>.agent.agent.task.assigned.<persona-slug>``;
#     per-message dispatch to the LlmCallHook with bridge-audit
#     reply emission + companion-subject output publish.
#   - OI-PEFR-7: ``wakir-mira-dispatch`` Side-CLI that mirrors Mira's
#     engineering Auftrag onto the Bridge-Forward-Pipe.
#   - OI-PEFR-8: Phase-2-Stub LLM-Call-Shim ``EchoReflectionLlmHook``
#     (deterministic echo responder; Phase-3 swap-point preserved
#     via ``anthropic_messages_hook_phase_3_stub``).
#   - OI-PEFR-9: ``wakir-doppelbetrieb-aggregate`` CLI for weekly
#     4-axis Bilanz (ADR-0058 §Pilot-Phase Schritt 10).
#
# Sprint-Pengine-9 closed substrate-gaps OI-PEFR-1..5; this image is a
# strict superset of 0.3.0-pilot — every code path the stub + 0.2.0
# + 0.3.0 consumed remains reachable. Quadlet tag-rotation (operator-
# hand) covers the 0.3.0-pilot -> 0.4.0-pilot swap.
#
# Tag-rotation pattern
# --------------------
#
#   1. Operator runs ``gh workflow run build-wakir-persona-engine.yml``
#      with input ``version_tag=0.4.0-pilot`` and
#      ``containerfile=Containerfile.real``.
#   2. GHCR receives the new digest under
#      ``ghcr.io/wakir-labs/wakir-persona-engine:0.4.0-pilot``.
#   3. Operator opens a Quadlet-pin-rotation PR updating
#      ``quadlet/wakir-persona-tomas.container`` Image= line tag
#      from ``0.3.0-pilot`` to ``0.4.0-pilot``.
#   4. ``resolve-image-pins-ci`` workflow fills the
#      ``@sha256:DIGEST_PENDING_*`` placeholder with the live digest.
#   5. Operator-Hand-systemctl-restart on the Pilot-VM picks up the
#      new image. Engine-swap complete.
#
# Wheel substrate (Bug-34c structural fix, Sprint-Pengine-9)
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Prior 0.2.0-pilot installed wheels via a flat ``RUN pip install
# 'rfc8785>=0.1.4' 'PyYAML>=6.0' 'shamir-mnemonic>=0.3.0' 'cryptography>=42'``
# layer (Mira-Hand PRs #66 + #68 to chase ModuleNotFoundError-at-boot).
# That layer drifts every time a new transitive dep lands; the
# structural fix is the ``[project.optional-dependencies]
# persona-engine-runtime`` extra in pyproject.toml. This Containerfile
# COPYs the repo tree and runs ``pip install '/opt/wakir-runtime/.
# [persona-engine-runtime]'`` once. Adding a new runtime dep (e.g. a
# future opentelemetry-sdk pin from Noa) becomes a pyproject.toml
# edit, not a Containerfile RUN-layer rewrite.

FROM docker.io/library/python:3.13-slim@sha256:e544a7fcbdf8555eceda66bf86cafb006c736339f76141918bcb812f3174c00a

# OCI metadata.
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.title="wakir-persona-engine"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.description="Runtime image for the Wakir persona-engine real binary (Sprint-Pengine-14 / Tag-52, v0.5.2-final-pre-cutover; Pre-KW-24-Final consolidation marker — manifest-and-metadata-only bump from 0.5.1-pre-cutover; strict superset of 0.5.1-pre-cutover with no new BackendDecision record, no flag rename, no flag-default flip, no crate-version bump; absorbs Tag-48 bridge-audit-writer wire-in PR #313, Tag-50 v0.4.2 DRIFT-S4 reconciliation PR #320 (Pin-Pack as SoT for spec §4.1), Tag-51 10-Decision-Engine-Resilience suite PR #327 (36 hermetic tests pinned-by-reference as the cutover-window resilience-substrate-pin), and Tag-51 legacy WAKIR_PE_*_BACKEND migration-detector PR #329 (Reza substrate, warn-no-fallback posture); 10 BackendDecision components ENV-gated under WAKIR_*_BACKEND, 15-crate Phase-3a cross-lang pin pack anchored at infra/persona-engine/pin-pack-0.5.2-final-pre-cutover.yaml, manifest at wirelang/persona_engine/MANIFEST-0.5.2-final-pre-cutover.md)."
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.version="0.5.2-final-pre-cutover"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.licenses="BUSL-1.1"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.source="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.url="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.documentation="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/blob/main/infra/persona-engine/README.md"

# Non-root runtime user (parity with 0.2.0-pilot + SPIRE-Agent + NATS).
RUN groupadd --gid 1000 wakir \
    && useradd --uid 1000 --gid 1000 --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin wakir \
    && mkdir -p /opt/wakir/bin /opt/wakir-runtime \
    && chown -R 1000:1000 /opt/wakir /opt/wakir-runtime

# Copy the wakir-runtime tree into the image so the persona-engine
# extra can resolve the wirelang package + setuptools-package-data
# fixtures. The COPY order is deliberate: pyproject.toml + the setup
# closure first (this caches the wheel-install layer when only
# wirelang source changes), then the source tree.
COPY --chown=1000:1000 pyproject.toml /opt/wakir-runtime/pyproject.toml
COPY --chown=1000:1000 README.md      /opt/wakir-runtime/README.md
COPY --chown=1000:1000 LICENSE        /opt/wakir-runtime/LICENSE
COPY --chown=1000:1000 NOTICE         /opt/wakir-runtime/NOTICE
COPY --chown=1000:1000 wirelang/      /opt/wakir-runtime/wirelang/
COPY --chown=1000:1000 wat/           /opt/wakir-runtime/wat/

# Sprint-Pengine-9 Bug-34c structural fix: install the wakir-runtime
# package + the persona-engine-runtime extra in one invocation.
# ``--no-cache-dir`` keeps the image slim; ``--no-deps`` would skip
# transitive wheels (we keep the default; the extra is closed).
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir '/opt/wakir-runtime/.[persona-engine-runtime]'

# Ship the real-engine entrypoint shim and symlink it to
# ``persona-engine`` so the Quadlet Exec= line is byte-stable across
# the stub-to-real swap.
COPY --chown=1000:1000 infra/persona-engine/bin/persona-engine-real /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine-real
RUN chmod 0755 /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine-real \
    && ln -sf /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine-real /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine

USER 1000:1000
WORKDIR /opt/wakir-runtime

# Entrypoint: the symlinked persona-engine resolves to the real shim;
# the Quadlet Exec=spawn --persona-slug tomas... line is byte-stable.
ENTRYPOINT ["/opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine"]
